To initialize a TypeScript project with Node.js, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the necessary dependencies:
   ```
   $ cd /path/to/your/project && yarn install --save-dev typescript ts-node @types/node @types/jest @types/mocha @types/chai
   ```

2. Create a new directory for your project (e.g., `tsproject`) and navigate to it in the terminal.
3. Initialize the project by running the following command:
   ```
   $ mkdir tsproject && cd tsproject && tsc -p ./tsconfig.json
   ```
4. Open the `tsconfig.json` file located at `/tsproject/tsconfig.json`.
5. Add or modify the configuration options as per your needs.

6. Run the following commands to start the development server:
   ```
   $ npx create-react-app myapp --template typescript:next
   $ cd myapp && yarn serve
   ```
7. Navigate back to the root of your project (`./myapp`) and run the following command to build the application:
   ```
   $ yarn build
   ```
8. The built output will be placed under the `dist` folder within your project directory.

That's it! You have successfully initialized a TypeScript project using Node.js and Git. Now that you're ready to work on your codebase, feel free to explore all its features and benefits.

